Subject: [PATCH] flourite: release temporary auto-brightness adjustments on AOSP

Zero is a valid temporary adjustment, not a release value on AOSP. Leaving
it installed keeps brightnessIsTemporary true and bypasses brightness ramps
even after Camera has lost focus. Pass Float.NaN when releasing the boost,
including the existing exception-cleanup path. Preserve the active 0.5 boost,
the app's zero-valued bookkeeping and the window-based screen flash.

diff --git a/smali/F1/x2.smali b/smali/F1/x2.smali
--- a/smali/F1/x2.smali
+++ b/smali/F1/x2.smali
@@ -286,6 +286,9 @@
 
     iput v0, p0, LF1/x2;->g:F
 
+    # Release the global adjustment without changing the app's local state.
+    const/high16 v0, 0x7fc00000    # Float.NaN
+
     invoke-static {v1, v0}, Lgq/a;->a(Landroid/hardware/display/DisplayManager;F)V
 
     return-void
diff --git a/smali/F1/L2.smali b/smali/F1/L2.smali
--- a/smali/F1/L2.smali
+++ b/smali/F1/L2.smali
@@ -323,7 +323,8 @@
     if-ne v1, v5, :cond_4
 
-    const/4 v5, 0x0
+    # Exception cleanup must release, rather than neutralize, the adjustment.
+    const/high16 v5, 0x7fc00000    # Float.NaN
 
     invoke-static {v0, v5}, Lgq/a;->a(Landroid/hardware/display/DisplayManager;F)V
     :try_end_0
     .catch Landroid/provider/Settings$SettingNotFoundException; {:try_start_0 .. :try_end_0} :catch_0
